---
// src/components/LiveEvent.astro
---
<section id="event">
    <div class="layout">
        <h2>Live event? Virtual event?</h2>
        <p>
            Too many events and conferences are hampered by poorly structured,
            difficult to read sites. Especially for mobile! <a href="/contact"
                >Let's help your attendees stay on track.</a
            >
        </p>
        <ul class="features">
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Planning and Design</h3>
                    <p>
                        Schedules, speakers, venue maps, sponsor tiers: we’ll
                        sort out what attendees need and when they need it, then
                        design a site that’s clear on a phone in a crowded
                        hallway.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Live Site Management</h3>
                    <p>
                        Events are fluid things, and things can change at the
                        drop of a hat. I can be on hand during your event to
                        update calendars, panel descriptions, and speaker
                        profiles in real time.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Hosting</h3>
                    <p>
                        Event sites get slammed the week of the show. I’ll set
                        up hosting that handles the traffic spike, and can spin
                        it down or archive it when the confetti settles.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>Integrations</h3>
                    <p>
                        Keep your site in sync with outside services like
                        Eventbrite, Shopify, and CRMs.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
            <li>
                <article>
                    <h3>See for yourself!</h3>
                    <p>
                        Our feathery friends the waterfowl don't get enough
                        love. <a
                            href="https://heroncon.netlify.app"
                            target="_blank">HeronCon</a
                        > is a conference that doesn't actually exist, but should.
                        At least it has <a
                            href="https://heroncon.netlify.app"
                            target="_blank">a cool website.</a
                        >
                    </p>
                </article>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    #event {
        background: #D6E6F5;
        color: #2B2D42;
        margin: 0 0 0 0;
        padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
        @media screen and (max-width: 750px) {
            padding: 2rem 0;
        }
        h2 {
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: normal;
            color: #14151F;
        }
        a {
            color: #B22E47;
        }
        .features {
            list-style: none;
            margin: 3rem 0 0 0;
            padding: 0;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
            gap: 1.5rem;
            @media screen and (max-width: 750px) {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            }
            @media screen and (max-width: 500px) {
                grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr);
            }
            li {
                background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
                padding: 1.5em;
                border-radius: 8px;
            }
            h3 {
                font-size: 2rem;
                font-weight: normal;
                color: #14151F;
                text-wrap: pretty;
                padding: 0;
                margin: 0;
            }
            p {
                font-size: 1.25rem;
                line-height: 180%;
                margin: 1rem 0;
                text-wrap: pretty;
            }
        }
    }
</style>
